2. Founder asks: 'LLC or C-Corp?'
==============================================================================
[law / text] hand_back=False actions=[]
An **LLC** is simple and flexible: profits pass through to the owners' personal tax returns and the paperwork is light, which suits a business you plan to run and fund yourselves. A **Delaware C-Corp** is what venture investors expect: it can issue preferred stock and stock options, and its law is well known, but it pays its own corporate tax and has more formalities. If you plan to raise outside investment, choose the C-Corp; otherwise an LLC is often enough. You're forming an **LLC** in Wyoming. Your 83(b) deadline is **December 31, 2026** (30 days after your incorporation date).

