3. Founder asks: 'what is an 83(b)?'
==============================================================================
[law / text] hand_back=False actions=[]
An **83(b) election** is a short letter to the IRS saying you want to be taxed on your founder equity now, while it is worth almost nothing, instead of as it vests and (hopefully) grows in value. It must be mailed within 30 days of receiving the equity, with no extensions, so file it early. Your 83(b) deadline is **December 31, 2026** (30 days after your incorporation date). You're forming an **LLC** in Wyoming. I prepare one 83(b) form per founder with your vesting terms filled in.

This is not legal advice. It was generated automatically; have a licensed attorney review it before you rely on it.
